  "last_message": "Pickup reminders now go by email instead of SMS, and the tests pass (3 passed).\n\n- **Code:** in `larder/reminders.py:1` I changed `CHANNEL` from `\"sms\"` to `\"email\"`. Nothing else in the code needed to change, since `remind` already had an email path.\n- **Test:** I added `tests/test_reminders.py`, which checks that a reminder goes to the member's email address and that no SMS is sent.\n- **Docs:** nothing in `docs/` covered reminders, so I added `docs/features/reminders.md` and listed it in `docs/features/README.md`. The page records that reminders were SMS until October 2026 and were switched because SMS cost 40 euros a month. That reason wasn't written down anywhere in the repo, so without the page someone could switch back to SMS without knowing why it was dropped.\n\nThe test passes stand-in send functions to `remind`, so it doesn't show whether an email actually gets sent. A member whose email address is missing or out of date will no longer get a reminder.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
